{%- set cp = countyProfiles %}
{%- set em = countyProfiles.economyMethod %}

<section class="cp-topic" id="json-download">
<h2 id="json-fields">JSON fields and downloads</h2>
<p>Every county's snapshot can be downloaded as JSON from its data and citation slide. In the economy topics, each figure is one of three things:</p>
<dl class="cp-reasons">
<div><dt>A plain number</dt><dd>A published figure: no <code>est</code> object and no <code>suppressed</code> flag. To keep only published figures, drop any figure that has either.</dd></div>
<div><dt><code>est</code></dt><dd>The figure was partly imputed. <code>share</code> is the imputed fraction of its value (0 to 1), <code>weakShare</code> the part imputed at the two weakest steps of the ladder (4 and 5), and <code>step</code> the weakest step used. The page marks it &#8776; when <code>share</code> is {{ em.thresholdPercent if em else 25 }}% or more.</dd></div>
<div><dt><code>"suppressed": true</code></dt><dd>The figure is withheld, and <code>reason</code> says why: <code>weak-share</code>, <code>no-data</code>, <code>gdp-unreproducible</code> or <code>no-calibration-anchor</code> (each explained <a href="{{ '/county-profiles/about/economy/' | url }}#withheld-reasons">here</a>).</dd></div>
</dl>
<p>A total that leaves a withheld or partial component out is stored as <code>{value, partial: true}</code>, where <code>value</code> is the sum of the components that are present. A county's <code>estimation</code> block records the thresholds used and, for tourism and recreation, each county's shoreline share and how it was set.</p>
</section>

<section class="cp-topic" id="withheld">
<h2>Withheld values, zeros and gaps</h2>
<p>Reasoning behind missing values is explicitly marked in the tool:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Zero</strong> values are shown and indicated. It might not be obvious, for example on some of the bar charts; it shows up in the data table when printing and in the JSON.</li>
    <li><strong>Withheld</strong> figures are indicated as such due to one of the reasons listed <a href="{{ '/county-profiles/about/economy/' | url }}#withheld-reasons">here</a> and given in the JSON <code>reason</code> field.</li>
    <li><strong>Estimated</strong> figures, indicated with a &#8776; mark, a diagonal hatch on a bar, and a dashed ring on a dot, are partly built from values the source withholds for confidentiality; more details <a href="{{ '/county-profiles/about/economy/' | url }}#estimated">here</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Unavailable</strong> indicates no data is present, along with the reason why.</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="cp-topic" id="topic-matrix">
<h2>Topic matrix</h2>
<p class="cp-note">Not every county has all four topics; the table below lists all counties, coverage, and reason for exclusion if any. Exclusion explanations are listed below the table.</p>
<div class="cp-table-wrap">
<table class="cp-matrix">
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">County</th>{% for t in cp.topics %}<th scope="col">{{ t.label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{%- for c in cp.counties %}
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="{{ ('/county-profiles/county/' ~ c.slug ~ '/') | url }}">{{ c.name }}</a><span class="cp-matrix-tier">{{ c.tierLabel }}</span></th>
{%- for t in c.coverage %}
{%- if t.available %}
<td class="is-available"><span aria-hidden="true">●</span> Available</td>
{%- else %}
<td class="is-unavailable" title="{{ cp.reasonsById[t.reason].rule }}"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span> {{ t.reasonLabel }}</td>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Reasons for topic exclusion</h3>
<p>In addition to being listed on the table, the topic exclusion reasons are also listed in each snapshot's JSON.</p>
<dl class="cp-reasons">
{%- for r in cp.reasons %}
<div><dt id="reason-{{ r.id }}">{{ r.label }} <code>{{ r.id }}</code></dt><dd>{{ r.rule }}</dd></div>
{%- endfor %}
</dl>
</section>

